### PUT /v1/projects/{PROJECT_REF}/ssl-enforcement

Source: https://github.com/supabase/supabase/blob/master/apps/docs/content/guides/platform/ssl-enforcement.mdx

Updates the SSL enforcement status for a Supabase project's database, either enabling or disabling it. This action triggers a fast database reboot.

```APIDOC
## PUT /v1/projects/{PROJECT_REF}/ssl-enforcement

### Description
Updates the SSL enforcement status for a Supabase project's database. Setting `database` to `true` enables SSL enforcement, while `false` disables it. This operation will cause a brief database reboot.

### Method
PUT

### Endpoint
https://api.supabase.com/v1/projects/{PROJECT_REF}/ssl-enforcement

### Parameters
#### Path Parameters
- **PROJECT_REF** (string) - Required - The unique reference ID of your Supabase project.

#### Request Body
- **requestedConfig** (object) - Required - An object containing the desired configuration settings.
  - **database** (boolean) - Required - Set to `true` to enable SSL enforcement, or `false` to disable it.

### Request Example
```json
{
  "requestedConfig": {
    "database": true
  }
}
```

### Response
#### Success Response (200)
- **status** (string) - A message indicating the success of the update operation.

#### Response Example
```json
{
  "status": "SSL enforcement updated successfully"
}
```
```

--------------------------------

### Configure Supabase Environment Variables

Source: https://github.com/supabase/supabase/blob/master/apps/docs/content/guides/getting-started/tutorials/with-nextjs.mdx

Save your Supabase API URL and publishable key in a `.env.local` file at the project root for application access.

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=YOUR_SUPABASE_URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=YOUR_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
```

